\describe{
\item{learner_timeout}{(\code{integer(1)})\cr
Timeout for training and predicting with a single learner.}

\item{n_threads}{(\code{integer(1)})\cr
Number of threads used for training a single learner.}

\item{n_cpu}{(named \code{integer()})\cr
Number of CPUs a single training of a learner uses, named by learner id, e.g. \code{c(xgboost = 1)}.
Overrides the default of the learner.
Must be at least 1 because the worker always runs on the CPU.
Currently informational only; the number of threads is controlled by \code{n_threads}.}

\item{n_gpu}{(named \code{integer()})\cr
Number of GPUs a single training of a learner uses, named by learner id, e.g. \code{c(xgboost = 1)}.
Overrides the default of the learner.
Can only be 0 or 1 for now.
The torch learners, TabPFN, and fastai default to 1; all other learners default to 0.
Only effective when \code{"cuda"} is part of \code{devices}; otherwise every learner is trained on the CPU.
When the requirements are mixed, the search space is partitioned into a cpu and a gpu subspace and
tuned with \link[mlr3mbo:TunerADBOSubspaces]{mlr3mbo::TunerADBOSubspaces}, see \code{subspace_profiles}.}

\item{subspace_profiles}{(named \code{character()})\cr
\CRANpkg{mirai} compute profile of the cpu and the gpu subspace, e.g. \code{c(cpu = "cpu", gpu = "gpu")}.
Must have the names \code{"cpu"} and \code{"gpu"} and the two profiles must be different.
Defaults to the profiles named \code{"cpu"} and \code{"gpu"}.
When the learners have mixed \code{n_gpu} requirements and the daemons of both profiles are set up with
\code{\link[rush:rush_plan]{rush::rush_plan()}}, the search space is partitioned into a cpu and a gpu subspace which are tuned
with \link[mlr3mbo:TunerADBOSubspaces]{mlr3mbo::TunerADBOSubspaces}.
The workers of a profile only ever propose and evaluate points of the subspace of that profile,
so the number of workers per subspace is the number of workers of its profile.
Otherwise the cpu and gpu learners are tuned in a single search space with \link[mlr3mbo:TunerAsyncMbo]{mlr3mbo::TunerAsyncMbo}.

